  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Righteous path Gu Immortals at Iron Eagle blessed land explain that Sword Saint Nian Er left a Sword Saint true inheritance with an extremely difficult and deadly test, so actual inheritors are rare. The inheritance is split into three portions. After the first round, obtaining the first portion, the inheritor is known as the Sword Child. Nian Er Fu confirms that Nian Er Ping Zhi obtained the Sword Saint true inheritance and was kept in the tribe for ten years before his first public outing as the newest generation Sword Child. Observers note that a new Sword Child true inheritor had not appeared in Nian Er tribe for three hundred years.",
      "chapters": [
        1106
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_righteous_path",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "loc_iron_eagle_blessed_land",
        "char_sword_saint_nian_er",
        "inh_sword_saint_true_inheritance",
        "char_nian_er_fu",
        "char_nian_er_ping_zhi",
        "fac_nian_er_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Even at rank six, a Sword Child is already treated as a force to be reckoned with among Northern Plains righteous path watchers.",
      "chapters": [
        1106
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_northern_plains"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Nian Er Fu later says every Sword Child in each generation is crazy, while still treating Ping Zhi as holding only a portion of the inheritance against a rank seven opponent.",
      "chapters": [
        1108
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "If the Sword Child progresses to rank seven, passes the second round, and inherits the second portion, that person becomes the Swordmaster true inheritor, a standing nobody in Northern Plains would dare look down on.",
      "chapters": [
        1106
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "swordmaster-stage",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nian Er Ping Zhi himself says he is only a Sword Child and plans to become a Swordmaster later when he cultivates to rank seven.",
      "chapters": [
        1205
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "swordmaster-stage",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The novel states a third portion exists. It does not name a third title in these chapters.",
